@startuml
title Generic Navigation State - Route-Based Beacon Guidance with RSSI Peak Tracking

[*] --> NAV_ENTRY

NAV_ENTRY --> SCANNING : load active RouteProfile\nreset RSSI history\nbestRssi = -127\ntargetSeen = false

SCANNING --> NO_SIGNAL : no known beacon\nfrom active route
SCANNING --> ON_ROUTE : PASS_BY or APPROACH\nbeacon detected
SCANNING --> TARGET_NEAR : targetSeen &&\ntargetAvgRssi >= arrivalThreshold
SCANNING --> GETTING_CLOSER : targetSeen &&\ntargetAvgRssi > bestRssi + improvementMargin
SCANNING --> WRONG_DIRECTION : targetSeen &&\ndropFromBest >= wrongDirectionThreshold
SCANNING --> GETTING_FURTHER : targetSeen &&\ndropFromBest >= gettingFurtherThreshold
SCANNING --> KEEP_GOING : targetSeen &&\ntarget visible within normal RSSI fluctuation

NO_SIGNAL --> SCANNING : continue scan
ON_ROUTE --> SCANNING : continue scan
GETTING_CLOSER --> SCANNING : bestRssi = targetAvgRssi\ncontinue scan
KEEP_GOING --> SCANNING : continue scan
GETTING_FURTHER --> SCANNING : continue scan
WRONG_DIRECTION --> SCANNING : continue scan

TARGET_NEAR --> WAIT_CONFIRM : show "Location found"
WAIT_CONFIRM --> SCANNING : ENTER not pressed
WAIT_CONFIRM --> COMPLETE : ENTER pressed

COMPLETE --> [*]

note right of SCANNING
Internal SCANNING logic:

If TARGET beacon is seen for the first time:

    bestRssi = targetAvgRssi
    targetSeen = true

This is not a separate state.
It is only initialization of the
RSSI peak tracking logic.
end note

note right of GETTING_CLOSER
Example:

bestRssi = -72
targetAvgRssi = -66

-66 is stronger than -72.
The player is getting closer.

Update:
bestRssi = -66
end note

note right of KEEP_GOING
Target beacon is visible,
but the signal change is too small
to trust.

Example:

bestRssi = -66
targetAvgRssi = -68

dropFromBest = 2 dB

This is probably normal RSSI noise.
end note

note right of GETTING_FURTHER
Example:

bestRssi = -58
targetAvgRssi = -72

dropFromBest = -58 - (-72)
dropFromBest = 14 dB

Feedback:
"Getting further"
end note

note right of WRONG_DIRECTION
Example:

bestRssi = -58
targetAvgRssi = -79

dropFromBest = -58 - (-79)
dropFromBest = 21 dB

If wrongDirectionThreshold = 20 dB:

dropFromBest >= 20

Feedback:
"Wrong direction"
end note

note bottom
Recommended thresholds:

improvementMargin = 4 dB
gettingFurtherThreshold = 12 dB
wrongDirectionThreshold = 20 dB

Use averaged RSSI, not raw RSSI.
RSSI is usually negative:
-90 = far
-70 = closer
-55 = close
end note

@enduml